{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.QDimNormalisation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.QDimNormalisation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Field","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.BallotNumbers","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.TemperleyLiebTower","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.TwoRowNormalisation"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QDimNormalisation.five_is_instance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QDimNormalisation.five_is_instance","kind":"theorem","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QDimNormalisation.lean#L232-L241","doc":"**The `n = 5` small case is an instance of the general one**, not an\nindependent check.\n\nRecorded so the small cases below are not read as the evidence for the general\nstatement. They predate it; they now corroborate it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QDimNormalisation.qdim_normalisation_general_int","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QDimNormalisation.qdim_normalisation_general_int","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QDimNormalisation.lean#L218-L230","doc":"The same identity with the **ℤ-valued** ballot numbers of\n`Mathlib.BallotNumbers` cast into `R`.\n\nWorth stating separately rather than leaving to the reader: it is the form whose\ncoefficients are the ones `ballot_sq_sum_catalan` is about, so it is the only\nform in which the `q`-dimension count and the Catalan count are visibly about the\nsame multiplicities. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QDimNormalisation.qdim_normalisation_general","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QDimNormalisation.qdim_normalisation_general","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QDimNormalisation.lean#L187-L216","doc":"**`[2]_qⁿ = Σ_k m_k(n) · [n+1−2k]_q`, at every `n`.**\n\nThe `q`-dimension of `V^⊗n` for the two-dimensional `V`, split over its two-row\nisotypic pieces: the left side is `(dim_q V)ⁿ` and each right-hand term is the\nmultiplicity `m_k(n)` of the shape `(n−k, k)` times that block's `q`-dimension\n`[n−2k+1]_q`.\n\nThe sum runs over all of `range (n+1)` with no `⌊n/2⌋` guard: past the last real\nshape the ℕ subtraction truncates the index to `0` and `qint q 0 = 0`, and at the\nsingle boundary index `2k = n+1` the *multiplicity* vanishes instead. Two\ndifferent reasons, one uniform range — see the header.\n\nHypotheses are the standing q-integer non-degeneracies: `q ≠ 0`, `q ≠ q⁻¹` (else\n`[m]_q` is `0/0`), `q ≠ −q⁻¹` (else `[2]_q = 0`). All three hold at the proton pin\n`q₀ ≈ 1.10998` with room. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QDimNormalisation.ballot_cast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QDimNormalisation.ballot_cast","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QDimNormalisation.lean#L170-L185","doc":"**The two `ballot` definitions agree**, `((m_k(n) : ℤ) : R) = m_k(n)`.\n\n`QOU.Mathlib.ballot` is ℤ-valued, because it is squared and compared against\n`catalan`. `QOU.QBeta.TwoRowNormalisation.ballot` is `R`-valued, because it is\nmultiplied by q-integers and carrying it in ℕ breaks Pascal at the boundary (see\nthat file's header for the worked failure). The two bodies are syntactically the\nsame recursion in different rings — and nothing connected them, so every lemma\nproved about one said nothing whatever about the other. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QDimNormalisation.coeffs_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QDimNormalisation.coeffs_six","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QDimNormalisation.lean#L150-L152","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QDimNormalisation.coeffs_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QDimNormalisation.coeffs_five","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QDimNormalisation.lean#L147-L148","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QDimNormalisation.qdim_normalisation_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QDimNormalisation.qdim_normalisation_six","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QDimNormalisation.lean#L127-L136","doc":"**`[2]⁶ = [7] + 5[5] + 9[3] + 5[1]`.** Coefficients `1, 5, 9, 5` are\n`ballot 6 0, 1, 2, 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QDimNormalisation.qdim_normalisation_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QDimNormalisation.qdim_normalisation_five","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QDimNormalisation.lean#L117-L125","doc":"**`[2]⁵ = [6] + 4[4] + 5[2]`.** Coefficients `1, 4, 5` are\n`ballot 5 0, 1, 2` (`ballot_values_five`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QDimNormalisation.qint_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QDimNormalisation.qint_two","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QDimNormalisation.lean#L93-L97","doc":"`[2]_q = q + q⁻¹`, the Temperley–Lieb loop parameter `δ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QDimNormalisation.qint_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QDimNormalisation.qint_one","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QDimNormalisation.lean#L86-L91","doc":"`[1]_q = 1`, given `q − q⁻¹ ≠ 0` (i.e. `q² ≠ 1`). At the physical pin\n`q₀ = 1.10997858…` this holds with room: `q₀ − q₀⁻¹ = 0.2090603`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QDimNormalisation.qint_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QDimNormalisation.qint_zero","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/QDimNormalisation.lean#L80-L83","doc":"`[0]_q = 0`. No hypothesis: the numerator is `1 − 1`. This is what lets the\ntail of the sum vanish under natural subtraction. ","signatureChunk":0}]}